  "name": "Faith and Belief",
  "publisher": "Initiative",
  "description": "For everyone who keeps something.",
  "long_description": "Ten symbols, one each, the same size on the same disc, in no order that means anything: a cross, a star and crescent, a Star of David, an Om, a dharma wheel, a khanda, a taijitu, a nine-pointed star, an ahimsa hand and a torii. The banners and the frames are deliberately not any one of them — a street where seven kinds of roof stand next to each other, a night when everybody's lamps are lit, five doorways all standing open, and two rings: ten symbols going round together, or two strands over and under the whole way. Wear yours. Or wear the street.",
